From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 03:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] capability: report the actual backhaul STA association

The Backhaul STA Capability Report populated its Client Info TLV through
get_backhaul_bss_info(), whose documented and implemented purpose is to
return an AP-mode backhaul BSS.  On a tri-band Agent this selected the first
mesh-backhaul AP, supplied an all-zero STA MAC, and let the Controller replace
the Agent's upstream parent with the Agent's own 2.4 GHz AP BSSID.

Use the existing get_bsta_bss_info() selector.  It requires STA mode,
backhaul haul type and an enabled radio/BSS, and returns the local bSTA MAC
and its actual upstream AP BSSID.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
+++ b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ int em_capability_t::create_bsta_cap_report_msg(unsigned char *buff, unsigned sh
     tmp += (sizeof(em_tlv_t) + static_cast<size_t> (sz));
     len += (sizeof(em_tlv_t) + static_cast<size_t> (sz));
 
-    em_bss_info_t* bss_info = dm->get_backhaul_bss_info();
+    em_bss_info_t* bss_info = dm->get_bsta_bss_info();
     if (bss_info != NULL)
     {
         // 17.2.18 Client Info TLV
